Topcom -- interface to selected functions from topcom package
*************************************************************

Description
===========

Topcom (see https://www.wm.uni-bayreuth.de/de/team/rambau_joerg/TOPCOM/index.
html ) is mathematical software written by Jorg Rambau for computing and
manipulating triangulations of polytopes and chirotopes.

This Macaulay2 package provides an interface for some of the functionality of
this software.

The package is meant as an internal package, to be called by packages such as
*note Polyhedra: (Polyhedra)Top,.  It is highly recommended to use those
packages, rather than calling this package directly.

Example use of Topcom
=====================

  * *note An example use of TopCom: An example use of TopCom, -- interface to
    selected functions from topcom package

Generating triangulations
=========================

  * *note topcomAllTriangulations(Matrix): topcomAllTriangulations_lpMatrix_rp,
    -- generate all triangulations of a point or vector configuration
  * *note topcomNumTriangulations(Matrix): topcomNumTriangulations_lpMatrix_rp,
    -- the number of triangulations of a point or vector configuration

Useful functions involving specific triangulations
==================================================

  * *note topcomRegularFineTriangulation(Matrix):
    topcomRegularFineTriangulation_lpMatrix_rp, -- compute a regular
    triangulation using all of the given points
  * *note topcomIsTriangulation(Matrix,List):
    topcomIsTriangulation_lpMatrix_cmList_rp, -- determine if a set of subsets
    is a triangulation of a point set
  * *note topcomIsRegularTriangulation(Matrix,List):
    topcomIsRegularTriangulation, -- determine if a given triangulation is a
    regular triangulation
  * *note topcomRegularTriangulationWeights(Matrix,List):
    topcomRegularTriangulationWeights_lpMatrix_cmList_rp, -- find a list of
    heights of a regular triangulation

Useful functions involving bistellar flips
==========================================

  * *note topcomFlips(Matrix,List): topcomFlips_lpMatrix_cmList_rp, -- find the
    neighboring triangulations (bistellar flips) of a triangulation
  * *note topcomNumFlips(Matrix,List): topcomNumFlips_lpMatrix_cmList_rp, --
    find the number of neighboring triangulations (bistellar flips) of a
    triangulation

Chirotope functions
===================

The chirotope of a point set (or vector set), consisting of the columns of the
$d \times n$ matrix $A$, is the function which assigns to each $d+1 \times d+1$
minor of $\overline{A}$ the sign of its determinant.  Topcom encodes this into
a string.  See *note chirotopeString: chirotopeString_lpMatrix_rp, for details
about the output of this function.

  * *note chirotopeString(Matrix): chirotopeString_lpMatrix_rp, -- compute the
    chirotope string of a point or vector configuration
  * *note naiveChirotopeString(Matrix): naiveChirotopeString_lpMatrix_rp, --
    compute the chirotope string of a point or vector configuration
  * *note orientedCircuits(String): orientedCircuits, -- compute the oriented
    circuits of an oriented matroid or point or vector configuration
  * *note orientedCocircuits(String): orientedCocircuits, -- compute the
    oriented cocircuits of an oriented matroid

See also
========

  * *note Polyhedra: (Polyhedra)Top, -- convex polyhedra
  * *note Triangulations: (Triangulations)Top, -- triangulations of polyhedra
    and point sets
  * *note ReflexivePolytopesDB: (ReflexivePolytopesDB)Top, -- simple access to
    Kreuzer-Skarke database of reflexive polytopes of dimensions 3 and 4

