Homogenize -- an optional argument to most functions in Topcom to indicate whether to homogenize the matrix
***********************************************************************************************************

Description
===========

Most functions in this package take a $d \times n$ matrix $A$, representing a
point or vector configuration: the columns are the points or vectors.  Topcom's
input is always a matrix representing a vector configuration.  A matrix $A$
whose columns represent a point configuration can be "homogenized" to a vector
configuration by adding a row of ones to $A$, forming a $(d+1) \times n$ matrix
$A^h$.

Functions with optional argument named Homogenize:
==================================================

  * "chirotopeString(...,Homogenize=>...)" -- see *note
    chirotopeString(Matrix): chirotopeString_lpMatrix_rp, -- compute the
    chirotope string of a point or vector configuration
  * "naiveChirotopeString(...,Homogenize=>...)" -- see *note
    naiveChirotopeString(Matrix): naiveChirotopeString_lpMatrix_rp, -- compute
    the chirotope string of a point or vector configuration
  * "orientedCircuits(...,Homogenize=>...)" -- see *note orientedCircuits:
    orientedCircuits, -- compute the oriented circuits of an oriented matroid
    or point or vector configuration
  * "orientedCocircuits(...,Homogenize=>...)" -- see *note orientedCocircuits:
    orientedCocircuits, -- compute the oriented cocircuits of an oriented
    matroid
  * "topcomAllTriangulations(...,Homogenize=>...)" -- see *note
    topcomAllTriangulations(Matrix): topcomAllTriangulations_lpMatrix_rp, --
    generate all triangulations of a point or vector configuration
  * "topcomFlips(...,Homogenize=>...)" -- see *note topcomFlips(Matrix,List):
    topcomFlips_lpMatrix_cmList_rp, -- find the neighboring triangulations
    (bistellar flips) of a triangulation
  * "topcomIsRegularTriangulation(...,Homogenize=>...)" -- see *note
    topcomIsRegularTriangulation: topcomIsRegularTriangulation, -- determine if
    a given triangulation is a regular triangulation
  * "topcomIsTriangulation(...,Homogenize=>...)" -- see *note
    topcomIsTriangulation(Matrix,List):
    topcomIsTriangulation_lpMatrix_cmList_rp, -- determine if a set of subsets
    is a triangulation of a point set
  * "topcomNumFlips(...,Homogenize=>...)" -- see *note
    topcomNumFlips(Matrix,List): topcomNumFlips_lpMatrix_cmList_rp, -- find the
    number of neighboring triangulations (bistellar flips) of a triangulation
  * "topcomNumTriangulations(...,Homogenize=>...)" -- see *note
    topcomNumTriangulations(Matrix): topcomNumTriangulations_lpMatrix_rp, --
    the number of triangulations of a point or vector configuration
  * "topcomRegularFineTriangulation(...,Homogenize=>...)" -- see *note
    topcomRegularFineTriangulation(Matrix):
    topcomRegularFineTriangulation_lpMatrix_rp, -- compute a regular
    triangulation using all of the given points
