naiveChirotopeString(Matrix) -- compute the chirotope string of a point or vector configuration
***********************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note naiveChirotopeString: naiveChirotopeString_lpMatrix_rp,
  * Usage: 
        naiveChirotopeString A
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Homogenize => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default
        value true
  * Outputs:
      * a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, 

Description
===========

This is a simple function written in Macaulay2 to generate the same output as
*note chirotopeString(Matrix): chirotopeString_lpMatrix_rp,.  However, it is
much slower.  But we wrote it to make sure we know what order Topcom is
generating the determinants.

+----------------------------------------+
|i1 : A = matrix {                       |
|         {0, -1, 2, 3, 4, -5, 6},       |
|         {0, 1, -4, 9, 16, 25, 36},     |
|         {0, 1, 8, -27, 64, 125, -216}} |
|                                        |
|o1 = | 0 -1 2  3   4  -5  6    |        |
|     | 0 1  -4 9   16 25  36   |        |
|     | 0 1  8  -27 64 125 -216 |        |
|                                        |
|              3       7                 |
|o1 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                  |
+----------------------------------------+
|i2 : om = naiveChirotopeString A        |
|                                        |
|o2 = 7,4:                               |
|     ---0++-+----+-++++++--+-+++++++-+++|
+----------------------------------------+
|i3 : om == chirotopeString A            |
|                                        |
|o3 = true                               |
+----------------------------------------+

