Caveat
======

With no optional arguments, this function returns all regular triangulations,
not all triangulations!

See also
========

  * *note topcomNumTriangulations(Matrix): topcomNumTriangulations_lpMatrix_rp,
    -- the number of triangulations of a point or vector configuration
  * *note topcomIsTriangulation: topcomIsTriangulation_lpMatrix_cmList_rp, --
    determine if a set of subsets is a triangulation of a point set
  * *note topcomIsRegularTriangulation: topcomIsRegularTriangulation, --
    determine if a given triangulation is a regular triangulation
  * *note topcomRegularTriangulationWeights:
    topcomRegularTriangulationWeights_lpMatrix_cmList_rp, -- find a list of
    heights of a regular triangulation
  * *note topcomNumTriangulations: topcomNumTriangulations_lpMatrix_rp, -- the
    number of triangulations of a point or vector configuration

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note topcomAllTriangulations(Matrix): topcomAllTriangulations_lpMatrix_rp,
    -- generate all triangulations of a point or vector configuration
