topcomNumTriangulations(Matrix) -- the number of triangulations of a point or vector configuration
**************************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note topcomNumTriangulations:
    topcomNumTriangulations_lpMatrix_rp,
  * Usage: 
        topcomNumTriangulations A
        topcomNumTriangulations(A, Homogenize => true, Fine => true, RegularOnly => true)
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Homogenize => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default
        value true
      * ConnectedToRegular => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,,
        default value true
      * Fine => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value
        false
      * RegularOnly => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default
        value true
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 

Description
===========

This function is identical in function to *note
topcomAllTriangulations(Matrix): topcomAllTriangulations_lpMatrix_rp,
(including optional arguments), but instead just counts the number, rather than
enumerate them.

For example, to use the same example as in *note
topcomAllTriangulations(Matrix): topcomAllTriangulations_lpMatrix_rp,:

+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : A = transpose matrix {{0,3},{0,1},{-1,-1},{1,-1},{-4,-2},{4,-2}}|
|                                                                     |
|o1 = | 0 0 -1 1  -4 4  |                                             |
|     | 3 1 -1 -1 -2 -2 |                                             |
|                                                                     |
|              2       6                                              |
|o1 : Matrix ZZ  <-- ZZ                                               |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : topcomNumTriangulations A == 16                                 |
|                                                                     |
|o2 = true                                                            |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : topcomNumTriangulations A == # topcomAllTriangulations A        |
|                                                                     |
|o3 = true                                                            |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------+

Similarly, one can count the number of triangulations with different properties
using the optional arguments.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : topcomNumTriangulations(A, RegularOnly => false)                        |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = 18                                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : assert(topcomNumTriangulations(A, RegularOnly => false) == 18)          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : assert(topcomNumTriangulations(A, RegularOnly => false) == #            |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|topcomAllTriangulations(A, RegularOnly => false))                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

